A||||50||FieroMike||Race anyone?
Z||000000||FieroMike||06-03-99||04:36 PM||||Just wondering if anyone here actually drives their Fiero!!  I hardly ever see any stories about racing other cars, or drag racing, or autocross.  I know you guys go speeding around the neighborhood, so lets hear about it!!!  <p>Just a thought - Could a Rebuilt 3.1-3.2 with competion cams, rocker arms, power pully, ADS chip, cold-air induction say around 260-275 HP beat a new LS1?  I say it could, though I would rather smoke a RUSTANG. (I can do that already)<p>Happy Driving!
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||06-03-99||05:34 PM||||Since most people have no idea what kind of car it is (here in Europe) and since it looks quite impressive, there aren't a lot of other cars that want to race with me...
Z||000002||87GT||06-03-99||05:34 PM||||Hey FieroMike,  I have only had my fiero for about 2 mths and the first race I had was last Saturday as a matter of fact.  I was up against only one car and it was a 95' Honda Civic SI. (I think)  It was a friends car.  He just got it and put an intake on it and did a few other things to pump it up. He has a 5-Sp like mine does.  So we lined up at a road nobody ever goes down.  I think we lined up 3 or 4 different times and each time, I would smoke him.  It wasnt even close to tell you the truth.  I always here how fast the Civics are, but on this day, the FIERO RULED THE ROAD!  see ya! 87GT
Z||000003||Eric||06-03-99||07:13 PM||||I got to autocross my 88GT once and ran rather quick for my first time racing.  But as luk would have it, I've missed the last three outing due to a leaky clutch hydralic system.  I got that fixed about a week ago.  Since then I been getting myself pumped up for the race scheduled this Sunday with a few races with Blazers, F150s, and such (In the farm country of Ohio it's hard to find anybody who doesn't own a truck).  Needless to say, I smoked them all.  Well, all that jumping on the gas pedal aided the clutch in it's untimly death just this afternoon.  I guess the best reason for the lack of Fiero racing stories, is that most of the owners on this forum do not own Fieros that run.  Too bad, they're a blast to drive when you can get them out of your garage.  <p>I'm going to do that 3.2 thing you mentioned, FieroMike, just as soon as I get the parts in.  I do plan on putting a power pully on and I already have a k&n filter element(I've done some research on the cold air induction and have concluded that it does very little for the performance of the stock or modifed 2.8/3.2.  Unless you could get a ram air effect, by inserting a duct into the airstream, you would be better off with the stock box).  <p>260-270 is a rather liberal hp estimate. On even the most heavily modified fuel injected 3.2, the horsepower is at most 250.  For my application and a few others on this forum, we chose to go for a modest 210-220hp.  This engine mounted to a manual gearbox could easily hang with an LT1 6speed or auto, but may have some trouble with an LS1 with the 6speed. (Even the base engines(non ram air)are under rated.  They usually put out around 280hp at the wheels, which translates to around 320 at the crank.  Thats 15 more ponies than advertised.)  Keep in mind, the 220hp I'm talking about translates to zero to sixty runs sub 6 seconds and for the manual trans mid 5 seconds.
Z||000004||Racer 1||06-03-99||11:24 PM||||I raced acouple of times against civics and integra's.I kinda spanked the civics but the integra with the 4 cyld v-tec or something like that spanked me good same engine thats in the type-r.Oh yeah one time a chevy station wagon spanked me at a stop light I quickly pulled into sonic to play it off! hehe but I like that looks of the fiero but them dang Iron Dukes just cant hang sometimes!  8-(  Laters
