Z||000016||SCCA FIERO||06-05-99||04:50 AM||||OK here goes. My 86SE V6 is rather "special" i guess. I say this because i haven't modified it in any way aside from the Holley scoop and K&N filter. The car turned in a time of 14.7 @ 98mph at sea level (i ran that in Louisiana and i now live in Utah) I haven't ran it at an actual strip since. It mostly ran about 15 seconds flat but 14.7 is the best i had. I hope nobody thinks I am makeing this up(if you live anywhere close to Utah i would be happy to demonstrate). I have street raced everything that would give the slightest interest. I have blown away Mustangs, Camaroes,Corvettes(not a typo)of all years except the C5 of course(havent had the pleasure yet:)and also 300ZX turbos. Except one 300. We took off hard and dead even, then i missed second gear. The guy wouldn't race me again and called my car something I can't repeat. I then got out of my car and walked towards his door. I guess he didn't want to stick around to see what I wanted because he then turned right. <p>My car, an 86 SE V6 4 speed, has never missed a beat and still runs STRONG. Too bad the car itself isn't like that. The result of 3 wrecks has made me decide to buy a better platform to work with. Today i bought an 88 coupe with a soon to be history 4 cylinder. I hope to inplant my V6 and 4 speed(or a 5 speed if i can't make my 4 speed work) and go from there. <p> I plan to race this car at the local drag before I "retire" it just for fun. The clutch is slipping and I am a little higher in elevation now so I don't expect a 14 second run. It should be fun though.
Z||000017||Phil||06-05-99||04:54 AM||||You have obviously never driven an AWD into a corner
Z||000018||FieroMike||06-05-99||11:03 AM||||Pretender: The GM sales brochure says that the Fiero goes 0-60 in 8.6 seconds.  When I got my car it was at 7.1 seconds, stock.  I know many stock Fiero's that can get under 15.0, I think it just depends on the driver.  Know what I mean? :-)  Plus the fact that they are turbo-charged and come out even with a Fiero.... ouch.<p>Phil: My woman has a 1998 Eclipse GSX silver, I have taken it into corners and it does well, but nothing like the Fiero. :-)<p>Plymouth Laser?  Do they still make those?  I can't find anything on the web about them, except some stuff on DSM.  What was the last year they made?  The reason I have beaten a Laser and not Talons and Eclipses is because I never run into an older Talon or Eclipse.  I seel early 90's Lasers everwhere.
Z||000019||Eric||06-05-99||01:53 PM||||I think the only years for the lasers were 1990-1993.  I could be wrong, but I think the lasers were 2wd only.  My friend bought a naturally aspirated laser a few months ago. And although I never raced him, I think it would have given my GT a run for its money (it blew up a few weeks ago).  The newer turbo eclipses and talons get to 60 in 6.4 seconds with a five speed and 2wd.  The awd cars take around 7 seconds.  The older turbos, believe it or not, can match the times of the newer cars even with twenty fewer ponies.  If you didn't already know, with a few aftermarket parts, these cars can do a 1/4 in well under 15 seconds.  So don't feel bad about losing a drag race to on of these rice rockets.   
