Z||000023||FieroMike||06-07-99||01:26 PM||||Yellow85,<br>I have the 5 speed on my FieroGT, the fastest that I know I have gone is 132, against a modded Toyota Celica on the highway.  That is what he claims we were going.  Nice races, I have beaten the Type-R's though, by about 1/2 a car length.  <p>Eric:<br>Believe it or not, I have raced several non-Turbo Porches, and won everytime up to the 70-90 mph range.  I think they are slow for the money.  The inline 6's on the Porche have almost identical stats to ours and they weigh about 100-200 lbs more.  Our Torque is higher though.
Z||000024||Eric||06-07-99||07:39 PM||||FieroMike, I don't believe you.  Unless you are talking about 944s, you are full of it.  First of all, the 911s have flat engines not "inline".  911s have almost always had a better power to weight ratio than a Fiero.<p>HORSEPOWER Porsche 911 <br>1967-  (130-160hp)<br>1968-  (110-160hp)<br>1969-  (110-170hp)<br>1970-  (125-180hp)<br>1972-  (130-190hp)<br>1973-  (130-210hp)<br>1974-  (150-210hp)<br>1975-  (150-260hp)<br>1978-  (180-265hp)<br>1984-  (207hp  U.S. models only, detuned and no turbo)<br>1986-  (207-282hp)<br>1989-  (250-?turbo)<br>1994-  (285-360hp)<br>1995-  (285-400hp)<p>If you ever beat a Porsche in a drag race, either the other driver didn't know it was a race, didn't want to ruin his valuable car, didn't want to ruin someone else's valuable car, sucked at racing, or didn't give his car the attention and matainance it needed to run properly.<br>
