Z||000029||SCCA FIERO||06-07-99||11:20 PM||||Yesterday I raced my new(to me) 88 coupe. I pulled up to the Tech. Inspection and my driver side seat was loose. I fixed it and then decided to take my 185/75 tires and wheels and swap them with my 215/60 tires and wheels from my 86. I went to break the lugnuts on my 88 and the third one I did broke the stud. I was afraid if anymore broke I couldn't compete in the 88 so I left the skinny tall tires on.  <p>My first run was pretty fast, but i went off course and it didn't count. <p>Then it rained. It came down so hard we stopped running until the rain let up. The track had standing water in several places and my bald tires didn't help any. My second run, my first in the rain, was FUN. There is a grassy part that the track went around with alot of spectators on it. I came around it a little too fast and the back end came around. I turned into the skid and held it sideways for about 70 feet through the 130 degree turn. AWESOME!! My cousin was standing in the grass and he said people were stunned I didn't loose it. This is fun and all,but not very fast. On top of that the rain messed up the lights and didn't time that run.<p>The next run was right after that one since it didn't register. It was still wet and slick. I approched the same turn at the same speed. It came around again and held it too long and slowed down too much and was out of the line for the next turn. This run registered, but i can't remember the time.<p>The next run was still pretty wet. I decided to take that turn like a civilized driver. I needed to get a fast time since only one more run remained after this one. I was pretty fast and considered this one was probably as fast as the wet track and bald tires would let me go.<p>This last run,usually refered to as the "balls out" run,was wild! Trying to go as fast as possible and have as much fun as possible. I went for the above mentioned turn faster than i have yet. The track was a little drier so I pushed it. I got SIDEWAYS and I mean the front of my car was facing the left side of the track. I let off the gas and it was corrected some then I turned into the skid hoping to get it straight. I turned too far and the front tires started skidding too. Then I killed a cone and the front tires got traction. When the front wheels lost traction I lost track of where they pointing. When they did catch traction it overcorrected. Then I was trying to correct a drift going the opposite way. Finally I regained control with only one cone down and still on course. The rest of the run was wild too. I knew the time was gonna be slow so I hauled A$$.<p>My fastest(third) lap was 76.9?? seconds. A 300ZX twin turbo in prepared class had a 79 second run so I think I did OK. I was in E stock/street tire class with those pesky Jettas.<br>
Z||000030||Patrick||06-08-99||12:19 AM||||<br>Remind me never to let you park my car... <IMG SRC="http://forums.gagames.com/forums/smile.gif"> <p>
