Z||000043||PaUL||06-12-99||01:40 AM||||This discussion brings to mind a prototype fiero I read about. It was built by GM in the 80s and had an all aluminum 2.9 v6 block with twin turbos. The engine produce 220bhp and went 0-60 in 5.8sec. It also had a sign in the back that said "Porche Eater".
Z||000044||FireWalker||06-13-99||11:50 AM||||Oh Sure, ya can do it with those souped up things.. =o)  How about Hanging with the Pack?<p>It's Saturday Night and FW has been polishing his newly aquired 4 cyl, Black, Fiero (just says Fiero on the back "shrug").  It's Cruise night in town and so.. he gases it up and hits the highway.  Not 10 minutes into the ride a MushRang blows by.. So.. Pedal down and we grab Tail light.. a few miles down the road and pedaling nicely FW looks in the Mirror to see a Black 99 Vette sway out into trafic and wham!  he is on the Mustang..<br>But.. Bringin up the rear.. needle pegged.. is FW.. pedalin' his butt off!  The Cruise exit comes up and all 3 get off.. hehe.. that Vette passed my car 3 times that night, looking at it sittin there shining.. Wonder what he was thinkin? =o)
Z||000045||lowCG||06-16-99||04:42 PM||||I think with the addition of a fiero in my stable,I'll keep on driving my trusty/recently replaced Jetta on a daily basis,and save the Fiero for special occasions,like visiting my friends who own much more expensive sportscars and who live in more remote areas.<p>After spending a day in jail(!)as a result of a NEG ticket,recieved from an incident in which I was driving the speed limit,hit(-and-run;victim),spun,and used the guard rail to save my ass from entering(backwards)four lanes of freeway traffic,with my 'lil sister in car,all on Christmas day,I no longer have any desire to drive fast on any road on which I can see any cars(assumably driven by complete f*%#ing morons)currently driving,or having any sidestreets for that matter. <p>Much less to show up some punk in a lowered front-wheel-drive wannabe sportscar.<p>
Z||000046||batboy||06-16-99||06:10 PM||||I haven't had my V8 Fiero very long yet and am still working out some bugs, but I firmly believe it could have beat my ol' souped-up 68 SS 396 Chevelle that I used to race in during my youth (the Chevelle could do 0-60 mph in 5 seconds flat). I have already spanked a yuppy jerk in a Porsche 911 with my batmobile Fiero though. It wasn't even close. I think he gave up in embarassment at about 60 mph (probably a good thing for me). However, let me say this, I never screw around in traffic or in town. That's nuts. When I let it all hang out, it's always on the open highway. That's the only good thing about living in Kansas I guess, plenty of wide open roads. Come on now, let's not get crazy and kill somebody or yourself. I'd like to visit Montana before they pass speed limit laws again. It's my understanding that right now there's no speed limits on the open road there. By the way, my other Fiero is a 4 cylinder automatic and it's terrible in the snow (I haven't and won't drive the V8 in bad weather). When the roads are slick, I park my Fieros and drive my old rusty, trusty, 4X4 Suburban. I thought they'd do better than that on snow with the engine sitting over the rear tires. Maybe it's the tires.
